></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mesa-del-nayar"><span class="enc-name">Mesa del Nayar</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mesa del Nayar is a mountain plateau in the Sierra Madre Occidental, in the present-day Mexican state of Nayarit.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mesa-vouno"><span class="enc-name">Mesa Vouno</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mesa Vouno is a limestone ridge on the south-east of Santorini, between Kamari and Perissa, that carried the ancient city of Thera.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mesalim-of-kish"><span class="enc-name">Mesalim of Kish</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mesalim of Kish was an Early Dynastic king of Kish who reigned around 2600 BCE and claimed authority over other Sumerian cities.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mesannepadda"><span class="enc-name">Mesannepadda</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mesannepadda was a king of Ur around 2500 BCE, named in the Sumerian King List as the founder of the First Dynasty of Ur.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mesara-plain"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mesara-plain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mesara Plain</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mesara is the largest plain of Crete, in the south of the island between the Asterousia mountains and the foothills of Mount Ida.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/meseta-central"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/meseta-central.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Meseta Central</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Meseta Central is the high inland plateau that covers much o